## 2. Methods comparison

| Step | Belykh 2022 method | This replication's substitute | Justification |
|---|---|---|---|
| Plant material | Col-0 + AS-12 (AOX1a antisense) + XX-2 (AOX1a-OE), 5-wk-old | None — substitute is independent dataset on WT Col-0 + *sog1* mutant seedlings | AS-12/XX-2 are lab-internal Komi/Syktyvkar lines (descended from Umbach 2005 constructs); no ABRC/NASC stock. Cannot be grown without an MTA. |
| Irradiation | Acute 200 Gy γ at high dose-rate, leaves harvested at 12 h | Scaffold uses 100 Gy γ on seedlings, 0/1/2/4/8/12/24 h kinetics | Scaffold is closest publicly available; dose and tissue differ — substitution is *directional* only, not quantitative. |
| Expression assay | qPCR with author-defined primer set on 27-ish target genes; not in supplement | DREM dynamic-segmentation paths from Bourbousse 2018 (microarray-derived) | Bourbousse pre-classified ~2,400 IR-responsive AGI loci into 16 dynamic paths (6 WT-induced, 5 WT-repressed, 5 SOG1-dependent). We test whether Belykh's panel genes preferentially land in WT-induced paths. |
| Normalization | ΔΔCq vs reference genes (not specified in abstract; full method paywalled) | Not applicable — using already-classified path memberships | Scaffold classification is the published Bourbousse pipeline; no re-normalization needed. |
